   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize certain health care professionals licensed to practice in\nother jurisdictions to practice in this state in connection with an event\nsanctioned by the World Triathlon Corporation; and providing for the repeal of\nsuch provisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8658",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8658-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8658\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize certain health care professionals licensed to prac-\ntice in other jurisdictions to practice in this state in connection with\nan event sanctioned by the World Triathlon Corporation; and providing\nfor the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation allows health care professionals to perform services at\nthe Ironman triathlon to be held on July 19, 2026 in Lake Placid, New\nYork.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Allows any person who is licensed to practice as a physi-\ncian, physician assistant, massage therapist, physical therapist, chiro-\npractor, dentist, optometrist, nurse practitioner, emergency medical\ntechnician or podiatrist in any state or territory, who is in good\nstanding in such state or territory, who has been appointed by World\nTriathlon Corporation to provide professional services to competitors at\nthese Ironman events.\n\nSection 2 -Provides effective date and date of repeal.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe triathlon in Lake Placid is a one-day, 2.4-mile swim and 112-mile\nbike ride which concludes with a 26.2-mile marathon, As this event is\nphysically taxing on the athlete, the health and safety of the partic-\nipants in the days before the event and especially during and after the\nevent are crucial. This legislation would allow licensed health care\nprofessionals from other states who volunteer and are sanctioned by\nWorld Triathlon. Corporation to perform services for the athletes.\nEspecially important at - Ironman events is the massage tent that is\navailable to the athletes following the race where muscle cramps and\nminor aches and pains can he attended to. Without this immediate atten-\ntion many of these competitors would require further intensive medical\nintervention.  The average time an athlete spends in this area is\napproximately seven minutes, which is not a formal massage treatment by\nany means. To service the 1,500 athletes, licensed volunteers from other\nstates are necessary. This event will be held on July 19, 2026.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nLegislation of this type has been passed by the Legislature in the past\nfor the Olympic Games in Lake Placid in 1900 and the Goodwill Games in\nNew York City in 1997 as well as for the 2001, 2002, 2003, 2004, 2005,\n2006,2007,2008,2009,2020 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017,\n2018,2019,2021,2022,2023, 2024 and 2025 Ironmen USA Triathlons in Lake\nPlacid.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed July 22, 2026.\n",
